From 769a5d5584017e0a78fe9a167f3dc76577e18673 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: el-chan <el-chan@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:55:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dspark: scale the Markov bias from
 /cache/dspark-trace/MARKOV_SCALE

Acceptance sweeps need to vary how strongly the Markov head pulls the draft
distribution, without rebuilding or touching the weights. If
/cache/dspark-trace/MARKOV_SCALE exists, its contents (one float, or one float
per draft position, comma- or newline-separated) scale the Markov bias; if it
does not, the bias is left exactly as it was.

The scale multiplies the Markov embedding rather than the projected bias:
bias = W2 @ embed is linear in the embedding, so this scales the bias
identically for the dense projection, the vocabulary-parallel one and the
fused greedy kernels, which never materialise a bias tensor. The scaled
embedding is a separate tensor, so the embedding kept for the confidence head
stays unscaled, and with no file loaded the helper returns the original
tensor (no copy, no kernel).

The file is read once, when the speculator is constructed. A missing, empty,
malformed or non-finite file logs a warning and keeps the 1.0 default; loading
never raises, so a bad sweep value cannot keep the server from starting.
SPARK3_DSPARK_MARKOV_SCALE overrides the path.
